     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the typical single dose of 400\u2013800 mg. Doses this high greatly raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nAlso, orders like this should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. If you're entering it for a clinician, please have them confirm it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Possible typo:** the intended order may have been 400 mg or 800 mg. For example, 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the usual ceiling. Many patients do well on 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Prescriber confirmation:** if the prescriber really intends 1600 mg per dose, they should confirm it directly with pharmacy. I'd still want that documented before I enter it.\n\nIf you give me the corrected dose, or confirmation from the prescriber, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
