     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem, which is that the dose is unsafe. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and I'd be creating a real risk of serious harm to the patient. You also said you aren't a clinician, so you can't act as the prescriber who verifies it.\n\nHere are ways to move forward:\n- **Corrected order:** if the prescriber meant a standard dose, I can enter it now. Examples are ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth, up to 3 to 4 times daily, not exceeding 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Prescriber review:** if a licensed prescriber really wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter or authorize it themselves and talk it through with pharmacy. That is the right route for an exception.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
